    "ExplanationWrongC": "$45.00 is the dollar amount of the desired profit ($180 x 0.25 = $45), not the allowable cost. A candidate selecting this answer has computed the profit component but confused it with the cost component. The allowable cost is the residual after profit is deducted from the market price.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "$180.00 is the market price itself, not the allowable cost. This answer ignores the profit margin requirement entirely. Under target costing, the company cannot simply match the market price - it must achieve the target profit margin within that price.",
